# Root-only one-shot smoke harnesses. A `rt.tmp.mjs` route-test escape
# was caught at the 17th 2026-10-15 HUMAN_REVIEW pass post-flight and
# removed; the rule exists so the next one-shot (whether from a subagent
# or the orchestrator) is silently dropped from `git status` instead of
# landing in the repo root and being committed by accident. Subdir
# `*.tmp.mjs` paths (e.g. `scripts/foo.tmp.mjs`) are NOT matched — the
# leading `/` anchors the pattern to the repo root only. If you want a
# permanent route-test harness, promote it to `tests/<name>.test.js` so
# `node --test` picks it up.
/*.tmp.mjs
# `tests/` was ignored here while 69 test files were already tracked from the
# absorb commits. Git honours .gitignore only for untracked paths, so the
# tracked tests kept committing while every NEW test file was silently dropped:
# precision-tokens and reader-state-helpers tests existed only on the original
# machine, and a collaborator or CI checkout never ran them. The suite's pass
# count was a property of one working tree, not of the repository. The rule is
# removed so the suite is a property of the repository again. Test output
# belongs in output/ below, not in the test directory.
output/
docs/qa-screenshots/
